# Strict Top 1 (1st) Auto Buy

`Auto buy` must follow top 1 (1st) optimal strategy: buy only the current top-ranked candidate, or wait.

- Do not add fallback purchase paths (e.g. 2nd-4th candidate) when top1 is not immediately buyable.
- Do not add "regret time", "acceptable detour", or similar heuristics that permit buying non-top1 options.
- If top1 cannot be bought now, return/skip and wait for recalculation; never force a substitute buy.
- Chain buying is allowed only for the same top1 target (e.g. buy-to amount), not for alternative candidates.

## Implementation Check

Before finishing changes in `src/core/**/*.ts`, verify:

- Decision path uses only `top1` as the buy candidate.
- No config or UI field implies fallback-to-other-candidates behavior.
- Any new optimization keeps the objective function consistent with "wait is part of optimal value".

## Examples

```ts
// ❌ BAD: top1 invalid => buy another candidate
if (!top1Valid) candidate = fallbackFromTopK;

// ✅ GOOD: top1 invalid => wait
if (!top1Valid) return;
candidate = top1;
```
